<speak>
<s>From <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news, this is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">22032026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="95%">
<s>Israel's defense minister ordered every crossing over the Litani River in southern Lebanon destroyed... a move that would seal more than one million displaced people south of the river with no way out.</s> <s>In the occupied West Bank, settlers burned homes across four Palestinian villages on Saturday, part of a surge that's killed six Palestinians since March began, according to the United Nations.</s> <s>Lebanese officials warned a ground invasion is imminent, while Israeli police are investigating just one of the settler killings.</s>
</prosody>
<p>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Iran's military command warned it would strike Gulf desalination plants if American airstrikes keep hitting Iranian power infrastructure.</s> <s>The Gulf states depend almost entirely on desalinated seawater for drinking water — an attack on those plants would threaten the survival of tens of millions of people across the region.</s> <s>Trump's forty-eight-hour deadline for Iran to reopen the <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="streɪt əv hɔrˈmuːz">Strait of Hormuz</phoneme> is approaching, and Tehran has shown no sign of backing down.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A US Patriot missile — not an Iranian drone — likely struck a residential area in Bahrain on the ninth of March, injuring thirty-two civilians.</s> <s>Both Bahrain and US Central Command blamed Iran until Reuters analysis by academic researchers traced the munition to a US-operated Patriot battery on Sitra island.</s> <s>Neither the Pentagon nor Bahrain has corrected the record.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Cuba's electrical grid collapsed for the third time this month as a US oil blockade enters its third month.</s> <s>The island generates just forty percent of its own fuel needs, and the blockade has choked off what remained — a stranglehold that echoes the worst years of the Special Period after the Soviet collapse.</s> <s>Havana's deputy foreign minister warned Sunday that Cuba is now preparing for a US military attack.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Russian recruiters tricked two hundred and fifty-two Kenyans into military service by promising civilian work — the men signed Russian-language documents they couldn't read, then found themselves on the Ukrainian front.</s> <s>Kenya's secured amnesty for returnees and a Russian pledge to stop recruiting, but one hundred and sixty Kenyans remain trapped in service.</s> <s>The pipeline exploited economic desperation in a pattern Russia has replicated across Africa.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Neighbours in Beddawi refugee camp in northern Lebanon are now thirty minutes apart.</s> <s>A Palestinian Authority weapons agreement with Lebanon gave Lebanese forces grounds to seal most of the camp's passages, trapping eighteen thousand Palestinian refugees inside less than one square kilometre.</s> <s>The Palestinian Authority itself hasn't challenged the restrictions it helped create.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Runoff voters in Toulon and Nîmes blocked Marine Le Pen's National Rally from capturing either city, uniting across the centre-left and centre-right to defeat a party that led both first rounds.</s> <s>Former prime minister Édouard Philippe also won Le Havre, positioning himself as the main rival to Le Pen ahead of France's next national contest.</s> <s>The results suggest France's anti-far-right reflex still holds — at least at the municipal level.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Slovenia's Freedom Movement won Sunday's parliamentary vote but shed eleven seats, finishing just three ahead of former Prime Minister Janez Jansa's conservative bloc.</s> <s>Jansa said he'd wait for final results before announcing his coalition strategy, leaving the country's direction uncertain.</s> <s>Weeks of coalition talks now lie ahead, with implications for Slovenia's alignment within the EU.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Washington's planning its largest war spending package since Iraq — Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth wants two hundred billion dollars for what he called "what we may have to do in the future" regarding Iran.</s> <s>Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent insists the US has plenty of money, but neither official has submitted a formal appropriations request to Congress.</s> <s>The last time American defense budgets moved at this speed, a ground war followed.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Pakistan tripled its premium fuel levy to three hundred rupees per litre on Sunday, but the tax targets only high-octane fuel used by luxury vehicles — ordinary drivers are shielded, saving nine billion rupees a month.</s> <s>The austerity goes deeper than the pump: the Pakistan Super League's been cut from six host cities to two, with spectators banned entirely under fuel rationing imposed after Iran closed the <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="streɪt əv hɔrˈmuːz">Strait of Hormuz</phoneme>.</s> <s>A four-day work week and fifty percent remote mandate are also in effect — the deepest peacetime energy rationing in Pakistan's history.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Australia's own fuel agency predicted a seventy-five percent supply shortage last May, and the government did nothing for ten months.</s> <s>The report, obtained under freedom-of-information laws, warned of severe damage to agriculture and logistics — yet no action followed until regional towns started running dry.</s> <s>The country that once thought distance made it safe from Middle Eastern conflict is learning otherwise.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Niger declared Africa's largest gas pipeline imminent on Sunday — a four-thousand-kilometre line designed to carry thirty billion cubic metres of Nigerian gas to Europe.</s> <s>The project stalled after Niger's twenty twenty-three coup froze ties with Algeria, but Algeria's state energy company Sonatrach surveyed the route this month.</s> <s>If completed, the Trans-Saharan pipeline would give West Africa direct leverage over European energy markets... a reversal of the usual direction of dependency.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>An enslaved woman's prayer to Venus has survived nearly two thousand years under Pompeii's volcanic ash — recovered by the Ancient Graffiti Project led by historian Rebecca Benefiel.</s> <s>An eighteen-forties German archaeologist dismissed all such inscriptions as trivial, halting the field for a century and burying the voices of the people who actually lived in Pompeii's streets.</s> <s>The project has now catalogued thousands of these writings, rewriting Roman social history from the bottom up.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Britain's Financial Conduct Authority handed Palantir access to its fraud and money-laundering intelligence, adding financial surveillance to a portfolio that already spans the <sub alias="National Health Service">NHS</sub>, the military, and the police.</s> <s>The US firm, co-founded by Peter Thiel — a major donor to President Trump — now holds five hundred million pounds in UK public contracts.</s> <s>A three-month trial will determine whether the arrangement becomes permanent, but the data's already been shared.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A single developer has rebuilt the nineteen ninety-six 3dfx Voodoo graphics chip entirely in code, replicating on a programmable chip what once required a full engineering team and a semiconductor fab.</s> <s>The project, built in <sub alias="Spinal H-D-L">SpinalHDL</sub> on a field-programmable gate array, is open-source as a template for reviving other extinct nineties hardware.</s> <s>Dead silicon, it turns out, can be resurrected — if someone cares enough to read the datasheets.</s>
</p>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="90%">
<s>That's your briefing from <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news.</s>
</prosody>
</speak>